 python3-astropy, python3-astro-virgo, airspy, rtl-sdr, hackrf
Suggests: hydrasdr-host-tools
Description: Narrowband SETI survey and hydrogen line for small dishes and cheap SDRs
 Point the dish, plug in the SDR, press Start. Aquila streams the receiver
 through a fine FFT, searches every block for drifting narrowband signals and
 keeps only the hits and small pictures. The same observation gives calibrated
 hydrogen line plots. Raw samples never touch the disk, memory is fixed and
 disk use is capped, so a node runs for months on a Raspberry Pi.
 .
 Works with Airspy, HydraSDR, RTL-SDR and HackRF. Several nodes can be watched
 from one desktop over the network. One install brings the SDR tools and
 the hydrogen line plotting (python3-astro-virgo, GPL-3, from the same
 repository) with it.
